{# P14 renders here. NC-A02 injector target.
   Jinja comments are stripped at render; HTML comments are not, and would reach the
   browser. Nothing in this file may contain a banned surface token — see
   cdfc.surface.labels and ci/no-green-tick.sh (registry row 1).

   THE TWO HERO LINES TAKE THE SAME CLASS. Same size, same weight, same ink — design.HERO_TOKEN
   and design.HERO_INK are single constants precisely so that a stylesheet cannot give one of them
   the accent and the other not. The line that would lose is the count of fields nobody checked.

   The reveal animates opacity and transform ONLY (docs/DESIGN-ADAPTATION.md, rule one): every
   row below is in the DOM and laid out before any animation runs, so a reader who scrolls past
   mid-stagger sees every finding rather than the ones that had their turn. #}
<section class="report">
  <div class="report__wash" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="report__hero reveal">
    <p class="hero">{{ failures }} failures across {{ checks }} checks</p>
    <p class="hero">{{ unchecked }} fields were not checked</p>
  </div>

  <p class="admission label">predicate set: {{ admission_state }}</p>
</section>
